# Pasta With Corn Zucchini And Tomatoes

Based on [https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/…](https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/11305-pasta-with-corn-zucchini-and-tomatoes) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251114013426/https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/11305-pasta-with-corn-zucchini-and-tomatoes))

{ rating="3" image="pasta_with_corn_zucchini_and_tomatoes.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] [Salt and pepper]{ ing="salt-and-pepper" }
- [ ] 3 Tbsp extra [virgin olive oil]{ ing="virgin-olive-oil" }
- [ ] 1 cup [corn kernels]{ ing="corn-kernels" } (from 2-3 ears) or 1 can
- [ ] 1 cup [diced zucchini]{ ing="diced-zucchini" } or summer squash (from 2 or 3 small vegetables)
- [ ] 1 medium [onion or 3-4 shallots]{ ing="onion-or-3-4-shallots" }, diced
- [ ] (Optional) 1[⁄4 tsp minced garlic]{ ing="4-tsp-minced-garlic" }
- [ ] 1-2 sprigs [tarragon]{ ing="tarragon" }
- [ ] 4 plum or [2 large tomatoes]{ ing="2-large-tomatoes" }, diced
- [ ] 1 pound [cut pasta]{ ing="cut-pasta" }, like Farfalle or penne

## Recipe

1. Set a large pot of water to boil. Put 2 Tbsp [oil]{ ing="virgin-olive-oil" } in a large skillet over medium-high heat and add corn. Cook, stirring occasionally, until corn begins to brown
1. Add [zucchini]{ ing="diced-zucchini" } and some [salt and pepper]{ ing="salt-and-pepper" }. Cook, stirring occasionally, until zucchini begins to brown
1. Add onion or [shallots]{ ing="onion-or-3-4-shallots" } and [garlic]{ ing="4-tsp-minced-garlic" } if you are using it. Cook, stirring occasionally, until onion softens (about 5 min)
1. Add [tarragon]{ ing="tarragon" } and cook for 30 sec, then [tomatoes]{ ing="2-large-tomatoes" }
1. Cook [pasta]{ ing="cut-pasta" } according to directions with shortest cook time
1. While [pasta]{ ing="cut-pasta" } cooks continue to cook sauce, reducing heat when [tomatoes]{ ing="2-large-tomatoes" } begin to break down. If sauce dries out (with plum tomatoes, this is likely), add some pasta cooking water, about 1/2 cup at a time
1. When [pasta]{ ing="cut-pasta" } is done, drain it, toss with sauce and remaining [oil]{ ing="virgin-olive-oil" } or butter, and serve immediately
